WEBVTT

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.020
Year 4 of the Ju'ei Period Dan-no-ura

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.900
The tide's changed...

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.740
The tide's changed! The tide's changed!

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.810
Minamoto-no-Kurou-Yoshitsune is here!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.150
Let us return to the capital.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:46.180
The people there await your return.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.190
<b>High General of the Genji Forces 
Minamoto-no-Kurou-Yoshitsune</b>

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.580
I'm not going.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.190
Kurou, I will give you this instead.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:11.020
Emperor, if you want to win, 
you need to survive!

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.250
I am Tokihito.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.310
In our capital, I am 
known as Emperor Antoku.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.310
<b>81st Emperor 
Antokutei</b>

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:54.890
How many years has it been since 
I've seen a warrior from the east?

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.440
Oh? That katana at your waist...

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.690
I knew it.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.090
The Ima-No-Tsurugi forged 
by Sanjou-Kokaji-Munechika.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.070
I remember this well...

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:13.100
Minamoto-no-Kurou-Yoshitsune's sword.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.910
<i>Minamoto-no-Kurou-Yoshitsune?</i>

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.960
I see. The talisman katana 
that I gave him then is now...

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.370
...protecting you instead, isn't it?

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.140
Teruhi?

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.060
I am honored to see you again, Emperor.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.200
No need for the formalities.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.270
Call me "Grandpa" instead, perhaps.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.830
Were you not aware?

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.110
Teruhi is my great-granddaughter.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.780
She came to see me once, long ago.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.950
Yes... When I was just barely a child.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.820
I don't know how you could 
identify me at a glance...

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.800
The Sou Clan lost many lives to the Mongols.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:10.890
But not all who know you have perished.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.990
I am one of those who remember.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.780
Your face reminds me of all of them.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:22.120
My wife, my daughter, my granddaughter...

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:25.820
You are, without any 
doubt at all, my family.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.340
Teruhi, take this.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.420
A letter to Magistrate Nagamine.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.870
Nagamine-dono?

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.840
Of the Toibarai?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:45.870
Yes. It contains orders to protect 
the people of Sasu and the capital.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:53.520
They did all they could 
at the Battle of Dan-no-ura that day,

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.650
but they failed.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:02.070
But one of those they fought 
to protect remains!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:08.200
As long as I live, they remain, 
in one sense, victorious.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:13.720
Teruhi, do all you can to protect 
the people of the island.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.210
If you want to win, you need to survive!

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.830
You have my word!

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.010
The Sou Clan were once part of the Heike.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.900
In the Battle of Dan-no-ura,

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.630
my great-grandfather managed
to save the emperor from death

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.260
and bring him to this island.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.270
My father was given the emperor's 
granddaughter to take as a wife,

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.250
and I was born.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:42.790
I see.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.450
I've always done my best 
to pretend the emperor doesn't exist.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:55.650
My royal blood made them 
call me the "noble child."

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:59.160
Even my father treated me 
like I was different. I hated it.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.640
But now I'm glad I have it.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:08.960
This imperial order will surely be a light

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.330
that protects the people 
of Sasu and the capital,

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.430
and all of Tsushima itself!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.730
You want us to rely on the Toibarai?

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.180
The emperor gave us his guidance.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:27.310
They make their camp up ahead, at Aso Bay.

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:31.900
But the Toibarai refuse 
to obey the Sou Clan!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.680
They've ignored our orders for years...

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:40.470
We'd bring shame upon ourselves 
by asking them for help.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.530
Enough!

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.170
It's far too late to be worrying about that!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:49.270
The Toibarai say they're the 
descendants of Japan's protectors.

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:50.410
What does that mean?

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.330
No idea.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.680
I don't know the details.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.220
Soldiers are all so stupid.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:00.020
They were sent to places 
like this and Kyushu

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:03.180
to defend Japan from outside invaders.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:07.180
But that was centuries ago.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:10.460
I've never heard anyone say 
anything to indicate they'd survived.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.960
But Kuchii-dono, even if 
they helped us in battle once,

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.590
will they provide shelter 
for so many people?

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:19.970
If it were me, I'd tell 
us to get the hell out.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.500
I love the smell of the sea!

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.650
So that's Aso?

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.210
When I went up Mt. Shiratake this morning,

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:33.150
I was able to get a look at the whole area.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:35.770
This bay has a very interesting shape.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:40.260
There are countless inlets 
in the bay, like a maze.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.730
They're impassible, which is probably 
why the main Mongol force isn't here.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.560
This lake looks like it's filled with piss.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.320
Idiot. This connects to the sea.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.430
I'm sure he doesn't know the difference 
between a lake and an inlet.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.340
This kid doesn't.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.840
Who the hell are you?

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.250
I won't let anybody insult our sea. Even you.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.540
Who are you calling a kid?

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.530
I dare you to say that again!

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.250
What is this thing?

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:11.950
Are you from this area?

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.880
A ship?

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:23.970
Are they here to receive us?

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:27.020
No, something's chasing them.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.650
That's...

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.240
Mongols!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.870
They're already here?

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:39.950
Hide in the forest!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.290
You said it was a peaceful sea!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.870
There's no such thing as a peaceful sea.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:48.120
It's all the same sea everywhere.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:51.930
Princess, let's hide in the 
forest and see what happens.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:52.750
Impossible.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.470
We can't abandon those women.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.610
So what's your plan?

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:01.030
Do something now, Jinzaburou!

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.160
If you want to do it, we can't screw it up.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.600
If we let even a single one escape, 
they'll find out where we are.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.410
We'll lure them into a trap.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:12.530
I'll strike with a bow from the beach...

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:13.270
Wait.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.130
They'll be fine.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:19.570
Almost there!

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:22.200
Don't kill them! Capture them alive!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.490
We're not letting them get away that easily.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.270
Search carefully.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.240
They're on the other side, as well!

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:46.960
It's a trap! Turn back! 
Get back into the sea!

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:53.780
Don't let a single one escape, men!

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:04.060
We'll have to swim back!

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:19.130
Will they allow us to stay 
with them, you think?

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:21.180
What's wrong, Genpachi?

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.070
Weren't you more concerned 
about the clan's honor?

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.600
What changed?

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:27.640
<i>But...</i>

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.610
<i>We have a lot of people who need shelter.</i>

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:34.130
<i>This may be a difficult negotiation.</i>

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.230
Hey.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.730
You survived?

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:42.840
We came to repay the debt we owe you 
when you launched that night attack.

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:45.570
Like hell you did.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:48.910
You came to make your debt 
even deeper, didn't you?

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:52.850
You did an amazing job as 
commander, Nagamine-dono.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.460
So the Mongols are here, as well?

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.500
Princess Teruhi...

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:59.300
That's the second group.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.180
But both were small.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:05.280
Fortunately, the Mongols 
do not yet know we exist.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.440
We've made sure none of them survive.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:12.180
That's why the fact that the Mongols 
are pursuing you is a problem.

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:16.950
Nagamine-dono, I come here as a messenger.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:21.110
I have come to give you 
the divine words of our emperor.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.650
A gourd...

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:32.240
I remember that, once, our emperor 
described this island as a gourd.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:52.740
We have obeyed the emperor's 
orders for generations.

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:57.730
Without his words, I would not have 
been able to convince everyone.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.140
You are welcome.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:04.870
I'm so glad you're safe, Tatsu-neesama!

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.280
Sana, it was fine.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.500
The abalones are a tougher opponent.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:12.790
Women divers, huh?

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.820
Hah! Women divers who are 
a match for the Mongols, huh?

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:19.820
You tie the wound to keep 
the poison from spreading.

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:23.800
Then immerse the entire body 
below the heart in water.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.520
Somebody carry them.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.720
Am I going to die?

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:29.530
I don't know.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:33.730
But you've been treated 
by the finest doctor in Japan.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.570
That should be good enough for you.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:38.550
It's good to have a doctor,

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:40.770
even if the rest of you are useless.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:44.330
<i>Mongols who use poison arrows?</i>

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:48.870
<i>These Mongols are different 
from the others as well, then.</i>

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:53.560
<i>Their bows and arrows are identical 
to the other Mongols and the Goryeo forces,</i>

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:57.120
<i>but they carry both regular 
arrows and poison ones.</i>

00:12:57.650 --> 00:12:59.670
<i>Their hair is different as well.</i>

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:02.130
<i>Perhaps they speak a different language.</i>

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:06.210
They're called the Jurchen.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.470
The Jurchen?

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.920
Or the "Toi" as well.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.520
"Toi"?

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.100
Well, you wouldn't know.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:20.990
Princess Teruhi, 
we will take you to our castle.

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:22.920
Kanatanoki.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.230
We've been walking for an hour!

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.120
How far up are we going?

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:47.630
Here.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:51.400
This is Kanatanoki.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:57.290
I've never seen a castle 
with such large stone walls.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:01.320
Never thought I'd see something like this 
on an exile's island at the ends of the Earth.

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:03.520
Did you build this?

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.990
No, our ancestors did.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:09.400
Six hundred years ago, 
in the distant, distant past.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.900
Six hundred years?

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:15.900
You act like the Mongols 
and the outsiders are a new threat.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:22.080
But the Toibarai have devoted our lives 
for centuries to battling them here.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:26.510
I'm aware this will seem rude,

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.650
but members of the Sou Clan,

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:30.550
you're going to have 
to follow our orders here.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.770
What?

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:35.720
Will Magistrate Nagamine 
suffice to lead them himself?

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.030
Genpachi.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.390
We don't have time to waste complaining.

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:41.640
But Princess...

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.790
Do not concern yourselves.

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.140
You'll be welcomed as guests.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:49.830
This place is amazing!

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:52.110
Look how far these walls go!

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.800
Hey, kid! Get off the walls!

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:56.680
How far do they go?

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:59.280
They go around and connect in a circle, kid.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:01.610
You again?

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:04.650
They say idiots, and you, 
kid, both like hiding places.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:05.830
That's "smoke" that likes high places!

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:09.420
You keep calling me a kid, 
but you're not that much older than me!

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:11.510
You're so scary!

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:14.300
Want to have a race along the walls, then?

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.780
We'll both run in opposite directions, 
and the first one to meet the other wins.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:20.820
You're a girl, and you think 
you can win a race against me?

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:23.240
Then the loser has to be the winner's slave!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.910
Fine by me!

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:26.570
Crap!

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.070
Aw...

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:32.080
Now come inside the castle, everyone.

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.550
It's so dark in here that I can't tell 
the difference between inside and outside.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.490
The castle itself is hidden, probably.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:48.500
Princess, some of the people 
have already escaped here.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:51.380
Their villages were 
destroyed by the Mongols.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.790
There was an attack last night.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.490
Hey, is that you, Obusuma Saburou?

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:01.590
Shiraishi and Kuchii...

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:03.150
You're alive?!

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.000
Yeah. You are, too, huh?

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.520
Where have you been?

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:10.770
Well, you see...

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:12.370
Who is that?

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:15.650
Who am I? You bitch!

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:18.150
You dragged me to this island!

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:20.610
Don't tell me you forgot!

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:24.650
Oh, the coward who ran before the attack.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:26.950
So you do remember!

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:29.090
And what the hell does that mean?

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.540
Let's have a chat later.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:33.250
Yeah, good idea.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.720
There's something I can't wait to tell you.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:43.140
It goes all the way up!

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:44.970
What is this castle?

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:46.130
The top!

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:47.990
It's still going?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.020
They surrounded the entire mountain?

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.510
That must've taken forever.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.240
Um... I win!

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:06.260
No, I win!

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:07.910
I ran into you first!

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:12.550
Um... Does that make any sense?

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.610
We're always going to run 
into each other at the same time.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.200
There's no way to tell who wins.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:20.100
You're right, in a sense.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:26.010
What was the point of 
this race you made me run?

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.300
It just exhausted me.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.210
What are we doing? This is so silly!

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:40.020
What are we doing?

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.940
It's been forever 
since I've laughed like this...

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:52.010
Me, too.

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:06.600
They have blacksmiths and artisans, too?

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.500
They seem to have a large 
stockpile of armor and weapons...

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.230
How did they make all of this 
without the Sou Clan knowing?

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:15.230
What's that?

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.280
Those are stone-throwers.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:21.710
It's a weapon that flings rocks, 
something we've used since the earliest days.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:26.190
I'd love to see them used sometime.

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:27.700
You'll get your chance.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:31.300
This place is incredible...

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:33.360
You took a lap around it?

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:34.270
What did you see?

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:38.290
It's so big, it goes up around 
the whole top of the mountain.

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:41.210
I'd say it's about a mile and 
a quarter all the way around.

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.520
A mile and a quarter?

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:45.850
The walls are tall, and there 
are a total of four entrances.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.210
Four...

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.320
Do they have enough defenders?

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:54.210
Hey, brat. Stop pretending you're a scout.

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.390
Who cares if he does, Gorouta?

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:57.840
It doesn't hurt anything.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.020
And his name's not "brat."

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.740
The kid's name is Amushi!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.360
Stop calling me "kid!"

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:05.860
What's over there is even more amazing!

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:07.820
It's almost a waste to let you see it!

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.530
What? Where?

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:12.340
What got into Sana?

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.720
She's totally different than 
when she went up the walls.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.800
That's a rare thing to see...

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:22.570
Is there some kind of legend that walking 
around the castle walls brings couples together?

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.640
Maybe I should talk a walk around 
the walls to inspect them myself...

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.090
Kano! Don't be stupid!

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.350
You take over here!

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:37.160
I'm going to check on everyone else.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:38.940
Princess!

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:44.710
We've prepared a small meal to welcome you.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:47.850
Black porgy.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:49.240
Dried and salted dolphin.

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:52.710
Kudzu soup with yuzu fruit, 
tachibana fruit, and sake.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.160
What do you think?

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:57.630
We eat the same foods 
as the people in the capital.

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:00.520
You're so formal.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:03.400
Look over there. They've 
finished tasting for poison.

00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:08.590
Sake! I'm alive again!

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:10.380
Stop it!

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:15.060
<i>It's been four days 
since we've had a real meal.</i>

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:18.070
<i>My stomach was getting 
sick of all that dried rice.</i>

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:21.930
You did an amazing job 
at the Battle of Sasu.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:25.900
Let us tell the story of Sou Sukekuni-dono's 
deeds until the end of our clan's days!

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.530
Thank you, people of the Toibarai.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:36.880
You took us in, but you took 
all the people in, as well.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:41.000
It's our job as defenders of Japan.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:44.380
Especially if the emperor 
orders us to do so.

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:49.440
This castle, Kanatanoki, is amazing, though.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:53.430
Indeed. Even their explosives 
couldn't break these walls.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:55.680
And you have the lay 
of the land on your side, as well.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:21:00.160
You could turn any Mongol that 
attacked into an arrow pincushion.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:05.800
We're simply using the things 
and lessons that our ancestors left us.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:08.890
If you do that, you'll be wiped out.

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.250
This castle's too big.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.610
Too big to be useful.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:17.660
I haven't liked you since the other day.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.620
You've got a problem with our castle, too?

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:26.260
You're never gonna get that much female
attention again for the rest of your life.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:29.300
Kuchii, what does that mean?

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:33.400
I took a walk around the walls, and just 
like I thought, you don't have enough guards.

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:35.520
It's so big, there's no way 
you can defend it all.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:38.730
It's like a child trying 
on an adult's kimono.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:42.780
If a large Mongol force finds this place 
and attacks, you won't last a minute.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:45.800
And what will you do to hold them off then?

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:48.160
This castle is a major threat to you.

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:54.630
Obusuma, what did you want to talk about?

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:59.690
Something I figured you'd be interested in.

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:06.070
I found a great way to get us 
the hell out of this place.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.970
<b>Episode 7: 
Kanatanoki</b>
